From bec6e261edcd00d9225cb95ef7e4a8e0b7298261 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JuggyMcNutty <11588877+JuggyMcNutty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:01:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] VM: an optional argument left out is not copied into the call

FORK ONLY. This project ships a NO-AI Code Rule asking that LLM-written
changes stay in a fork and are never PR'd upstream. These were written with
Claude. Do not submit them.

A script call that leaves out an optional parameter passes a Nothing value
for it, and Frame::CallScript stored every argument into the new frame.
For a scalar that stored a zero; for a struct or an array
ExpressionValue::Store copies field by field from the argument's pointer,
which a Nothing value does not have: a crash. ScriptedPawn's
ComputeBestFiringPosition calls TryLocation(tryVector, minDist) without its
struct projList, so the first Deus Ex NPC to attack crashed the engine
(upstream too). An argument left out now keeps what the frame gave it, zero
or the type's default, as UE1 leaves it.

Checked: an NSF terrorist turned on the player in Liberty Island, ran
Attacking's firing-position code and went on shooting, where it had crashed
at that call.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 SurrealEngine/VM/Frame.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/SurrealEngine/VM/Frame.cpp b/SurrealEngine/VM/Frame.cpp
index 3f0b18a..d2cb566 100644
--- a/SurrealEngine/VM/Frame.cpp
+++ b/SurrealEngine/VM/Frame.cpp
@@ -283,9 +283,13 @@ ExpressionValue Frame::CallScript(UFunction* func, UObject* instance, CallArgume
 	Frame frame(instance, func);
 	const Array<UProperty*>& parms = func->CallParms;
 
-	// Store args in function frame local variables
+	// Store args in function frame local variables. An optional argument the
+	// caller left out keeps the value the frame gave it, zero, as in UE1: a
+	// struct or an array would be copied from nothing.
 	for (size_t i = 0; i < parms.size() && i < args.size(); i++)
 	{
+		if (args[i].GetType() == ExpressionValueType::Nothing)
+			continue;
 		ExpressionValue lvalue = ExpressionValue::Variable(frame.Variables.Data, parms[i]);
 		lvalue.Store(args[i]);
 	}
